{
  "name": "pump_flow_control_zero_flow_reopen",
  "description": "A flow-controlled pump and its discharge check valve feed a junction whose only outlet is through a PRV. The PRV starts active and leaves the junction without a fixed head, so the pump starts at maximum speed while an FCV with an unreachable setpoint forces more flow into the junction than the PRV passes: the surplus flows back through the pump line and the pump and check valve close together. Verifies that they are re-tested against the pump's zero-flow bound at maximum speed (not minimum speed), re-open, and the pump then holds its setpoint with both control valves fully open, at the closed-form values.",
  "source": "closed-form: tests/reference/derivations_pump_control.py::pump_flow_control_zero_flow_reopen (flow control (proposal vfd-pump-modes.md 2.4, 4.5): active Q = Q_set with s* from s*^2 H0(Q_set/s*) = EGL_d - EGL_s; at a limit the fixed-speed pump at s_max or s_min; pump curve: scipy PchipInterpolator, linear end-slope extension, affinity laws; check-valve K from fluids K_swing_check_valve_Crane (angled); FCV and PRV fully open and ideal; FCV line flow by brentq; s* by brentq on H0(x) = (H/Q^2) x^2; first-solve PRV flow from z + p/(rho g) + v^2/2g by brentq; line fittings: fluids entrance_sharp(method='Crane'), exit_normal())",
